WEBVTT

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:08.530
(AMBASSADOR GRUNTS)

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.210
(BOTH GRUNTING)

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.850
ELASTIGIRL: We're gonna have
to slingshot! Hang on!

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.890
-(ELASTIGIRL GRUNTING)
-(AMBASSADOR SCREAMING)

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:26.650
-(PANTING)
-Are you all right, ma'am?

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:28.490
I'm perfectly fine...

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:32.210
BOB: Ah! Ooh! Ah! Oh!

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:40.970
Boys are jerks
and superheroes suck.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:42.170
Good morning!

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.290
He takes one look
at me in that suit...

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:48.130
and decides to pretend
he doesn't even know me.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:50.290
He's protecting himself.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.090
If he really did see you,
it's best that he forget.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.010
It's better for you, too.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.210
I can't tell you
how many memories

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.570
Dicker's had to erase
over the years...

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.410
(SNIFFS)
when someone figured out

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.090
your mother's or my identity.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:05.610
-(GASPS)
-It was Dicker!

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.970
-You told him about Tony!
-Honey...

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.690
You had me erased
from Tony's mind!

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:16.570
(DOOR SLAMS)

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.690
-(JACK-JACK GIGGLING)
-(DOOR OPENS)

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:25.890
I hate superheroes!

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:27.930
And I renounce them!

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:29.850
(WHIRRING)

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.050
I renounce them!

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:37.930
(GRUNTING)

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:42.010
(PANTING)

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:44.370
(FOOTSTEPS RETREATING)

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:47.730
-Is she having adolescence?
-(DOOR SLAMS)

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:49.410
REPORTER: A new report
out today shows that,

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:51.330
when it comes
to decision-making...

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:53.170
people have more trust
in a monkey

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:54.610
throwing darts than Congress.

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:56.930
What's going on, Tommy?
A protest?

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:58.770
-(PROTESTERS CHANTING)
-They're here in support.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:01.010
Support? Support of what?

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:03.330
TOMMY:
Well, in support of you.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:05.170
(CHANTING CONTINUES)

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:08.810
Wow. Oh, hey...

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:11.050
Thanks for coming out. Hi.

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:13.890
Oh, my goodness.
Thanks so much.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:15.330
Oh, hello.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:16.850
What does your sign say?

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:22.810
ALL: (CHANTING)
Ka-boom! Ka-pow!

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:24.690
Supers should be legal now!

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.570
Talk to ya.
Oh, what do ya know!

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:28.970
Ellenwood.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:30.850
Oh, now you wanna
return my calls

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:31.930
about superheroes, huh?

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.890
Oh. I'll have to
call you back.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:35.090
Oh, that felt good.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.530
Felicia, hold my calls,
please.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:38.210
Hey!
It's working!

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.490
Hey, the ambassador
made a big speech

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:41.690
about superheroes today.

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:43.170
Turns out
saving someone's life

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.970
makes a good impression
on them. Who knew, huh?

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:47.170
I'm getting calls
from all over the world.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:49.810
Media awareness is up 72%.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:52.050
The push
for superhero legalization

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:53.930
is becoming
a worldwide movement!

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:55.810
I have big plans
for our next move.

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:57.610
We're gonna have
a summit at sea.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:58.690
We'll use our ship...

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:01.050
we'll gather leaders
and Supers...

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:03.410
-from all over the world.
-That's great.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:04.850
I'm happy.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.370
I'm happy the numbers are up.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:09.490
I'm happy the ambassador
is pro-superhero...

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:11.370
and I'm happy you're happy.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:14.530
I'm hearing that you're happy,
but why am I not feeling it?

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:16.210
Because I didn't get him!

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.370
Screenslaver
is still out there.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.490
All I did was play his game
and win this round.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:21.730
He's gonna want more

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:24.010
and as long as
he gets to play, he wins.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.810
One thing
I've learned in business?

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.730
Smell the flowers.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:29.250
They don't bloom that often.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:30.850
What do you want
on your tombstone?

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:31.930
"She worried a lot"?

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:33.570
EVELYN: All right,
stop talking.

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:35.170
Show her.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:40.450
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:43.450
This is just
so exciting, isn't it? Huh?

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.490
(CHATTER STOPS)

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.370
Oh, wow. Uh...

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:50.570
Wow! Elastigirl,
there you are.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.010
-Hello.
-(STAMMERS) I didn't...

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:53.290
Wow!

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.410
Come on,
get yourself together, Karen.

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:59.130
Hi, my superhero name is Voyd.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:02.970
I just wanna thank you,
for, like, for being you!

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:05.130
(STAMMERING)

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:08.290
Okay, what I can do, um,
is this.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.370
(ALL GASP)

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.690
(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY) Yeah.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:19.290
That is impressive.
Very interdimensional.

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:21.610
I felt like an outcast before.

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:25.810
But now, with you being you,
I feel like...

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:27.650
(SIGHS)

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:28.770
Yay, me.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:31.890
I flew them in from all over.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:33.690
They've all been in hiding.

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:35.970
They have powers,
secret identities...

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:38.130
and names
they've given themselves.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:41.010
I'm Screech. It's a pleasure.

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.410
I've always considered you

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.450
the gold standard
for superheroes.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.610
Well, thanks. You're too nice.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:48.490
I am called Brick.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:51.850
Nice to meet you, Brick.
Uh, where are you from?

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:53.330
Wisconsin.

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:56.610
Oh. Elastigirl.
I assume your powers are...

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.010
You know,
zapping things electrically...

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:01.290
charging things, bolts of
lightning, that kind of stuff.

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:02.690
Name's Reflux.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:06.050
Medical condition
or superpower, you decide.

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:07.490
(CHUCKLES)
That's a little line

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:08.810
I say just to put
people at ease.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:10.010
Hope I don't offend.

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:12.050
Oh, no, no, no.
Reflux. Love it.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:13.330
(JAZZ MUSIC PLAYING)

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.050
Well, I do look forward
to working with you.

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:19.490
Yes, that is impressive.
Keep practicing.

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:21.090
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.370
-(ELECTRICITY CRACKLES)
-Ow!

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:23.850
(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:25.290
(SNORING)

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:28.850
Well, I'm beat.
Congratulations. Big day.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:31.210
Good night, ladies.
I will see you tomorrow.

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:32.370
Good night.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:34.290
Must be nice for you,

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:35.890
being out front
after all this time.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:37.090
Out front?

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:40.090
Well, it's been a while
since your superhero days...

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:42.130
and even then,
you were kind of

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.410
in Mr. Incredible's shadow.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:45.090
Nah, I beg to differ.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:47.090
I'm not... I'm not
saying you weren't big.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:49.130
No, you were,
and are, a superstar...

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:52.010
but you have
the stage to yourself now.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:54.050
And people have
to pay attention.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:55.770
Oh, you mean, "It's a man's
world" and all that?

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:57.650
Well, what world
do you live in?

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:59.090
Your brother runs DEVTECH.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:03.290
I don't want his job.
I invent, he sells.

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:06.610
I ask you, which of us
has the greater influence?

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:08.210
Which side of me
are you asking?

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:09.530
The believer or the cynic?

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:10.690
The cynic...

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:12.370
Would say selling
is more important

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:14.570
because the best sellers
have the most buyers.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.330
Doesn't matter
what you're selling.

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:18.170
It only matters
what people buy.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:19.370
This is true.

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:21.890
If I discovered
the origin of the universe...

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:23.410
my brother would find a way

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:26.330
to market it as a, uh,
foot massager.

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:28.250
(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:30.650
So, what would
the believer say?

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:33.170
The believer would tell you
to make your mark.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.450
Don't wait for permission,
assert yourself

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:37.090
and impose your will
on the status quo.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.890
-Sounds like my brother.
-What?

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:40.130
You sound like my brother.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:41.370
Well, he's not wrong.

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:43.090
There is an art
to getting a reaction...

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:44.530
(GASPS) Oh! I know
how to get him.

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:47.610
-My brother?
-No. Screenslaver!

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:50.290
You're tech-savvy. I need
to lock onto a signal...

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:51.530
and trace its origin.

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:52.770
How fast can you
slap something together

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:53.890
and meet me at the airport?

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.010
Airport?

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:56.370
Need to go
out of town, pronto.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:58.010
I can get your contraption
together by 5:00 a.m.

00:06:58.170 --> 00:07:00.050
I need to get on TV.
Chad!

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:01.890
I'll get my brother to set up
an exclusive with him

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:02.970
tonight on the newscast.

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:04.170
Finish our interview by phone!

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:05.250
Promote the hell out of it.

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:06.970
Independence
from Screenslavery!

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:09.330
-Chad tonight.
-BOTH: Boom! (LAUGHING)

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:11.290
(PHONE RINGING)

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:14.490
-Dicker.
-BOB: Yeah, hey, Rick.

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:16.210
You remember that kid
I mentioned to you?

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.330
Tony Rydinger.

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:19.170
Mind wipe? Yeah, nice kid.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.010
Well, you also wiped out

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:22.930
the Friday night date
my daughter had with him.

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:25.370
In fact,
you wiped out my daughter.

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:27.770
Oops.
Not an exact science, Bob.

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:29.570
Rick, you gotta help me here.

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:32.650
Violet hates me, and you,
and superheroes.

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:35.250
I gotta fix this.
What do you know about Tony?

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:36.570
Um...

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:37.970
Not much.

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:39.610
Seems like a good kid.

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:41.890
Popular, plays sports, music.

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:45.450
Parents own The Happy Platter,
kid works there part time.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:47.810
Happy Platter?

